skew-insensitive) vs precision vs recall (skew-sensitive)."],["Logit vs logistic","log(p/(1 − p)) vs 1/(1 + e^(−z)): inverses."]],"minute":"Classification assigns the class with the highest posterior; regions where classes overlap produce unavoidable error. Logistic regression models P(y = 1|x) = σ(θᵀx), so the boundary is θᵀx = 0 and each coefficient multiplies the odds by e^θ. It is trained by minimising convex cross-entropy with gradient descent, whose update (h − y)x matches linear regression's. Evaluate with the confusion matrix: precision, recall, F1, specificity and FPR, plus ROC/AUC across thresholds. With rare classes, avoid accuracy, rebalance training data and tune the threshold. For many classes use one-vs-rest or one-vs-one."},"flashcards":[["Bayes decision rule","Choose the class with the largest posterior p(C|x)",9],["Generative vs discriminative","Model p(x|c)p(c) vs model p(c|x) or boundary",12],["Sigmoid","$g(z)=\\frac1{1+e^{-z}}$, $g'=g(1-g)$",20],["Logistic hypothesis","$h_\\theta(x)=\\frac1{1+e^{-\\theta^\\top x}}$",20],["Log-odds","$\\ln\\frac p{1-p}=\\theta^\\top x$",21],["Decision boundary","$\\theta^\\top x=0$ (h = 0.5)",22],["Cross-entropy","$J=-\\frac1m\\sum[y\\log h+(1-y)\\log(1-h)]$",29],["Logistic GD update","$\\theta_j\\leftarrow\\theta_j-\\alpha\\frac1m\\sum(h-y)x_j$",30],["Odds ratio","$e^{\\theta_j}$ per unit increase in $x_j$",37],["sklearn C","Inverse regularisation strength",39],["Precision / recall","TP/(TP+FP) / TP/(TP+FN)",43],["F1","2pr/(p + r)",43],["FPR / specificity","FP/(FP+TN) = 1 − TN/(TN+FP)",43],["ROC landmarks","(0,1) ideal; diagonal random; AUC 1 perfect, 0.5 random",48],["OvR vs OvO count","K models vs K(K−1)/2",61]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["c-decision"],"viz":["rocThreshold"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["c-types"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3","why"],"deep":["c-ls"],"viz":["lsVsLogit"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["c-sigmoid"],"viz":["sigmoi